From 5265a6eaa9e57e40a4daad40a4247477bed34e9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mj <mj@maxlinear.com>
Date: Wed, 20 Aug 2025 00:27:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-92433 ZWDFS retrieves the second-best channel
 without rewriting the ACS smart file again

Current implementation:
The DFS channel monitoring should happen continuously in the background for the next best DFS channel to clear the CAC.
update the DFS channel state (usable or available or unavailable) During radar hit, do not switch to non-DFS immediately,
switch to the second best available DFS channel immediately.
to select second best channel trigger acs recal function again.

Proposed design:
Few info correpted in acs_smart file. so, we don't want to use acs_recal function to get second best channel.
Hence, used existing acs table to retrive second best channel.

Few other issue is resolved as part this commit.
Issue 1: WLANRTSYS-92970 second best channel is not valid as per ACS ranking.
Fix: currently, overlapping channel gets skipped before select second best channel. to compare overlap channel, used freq from acs candidate and compared with current operating freq. But, freq is not valid in the acs candidate table. only lower channel frequency is updated in acs table which we should not use for channel overlap comparison. So, convert freq from channel and
width and compared the overlapping channel. now, second best channel selection should be valid.

Issue 2: WLANRTSYS-90721 ACS file is not same
Fix : not using acs reacl function to retrive second best channel again. so , acs table is proper now.

Issue 3: WLANRTSYS-93150 false radar detection
Fix: Don't select the second best channel , if ACS select non DFS at init.
